(1. Open your target Google Sheet database in Google Drive.) Tj
T* (2. Go to Extensions > Apps Script, paste the bridge script and click Save.) Tj
T* (3. Click Deploy > New deployment, choose Web App, set Execute as 'Me' and Who has access to 'Anyone'.) Tj
T* (4. Deploy, authorize Google access, copy the Web App URL and set it in VITE_GOOGLE_SHEETS_WEB_APP_URL.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 14 Tf
16.0999999999999979 TL
0.059 0.298 0.506 rg
42.5196850393700814 657.6380314960629221 Td
(4. Site Deployment & Launch Guide) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.298 0.506 rg
42.5196850393700814 629.291574803149615 Td
(4.1 Vercel Hosting Setup \(Exclusive Host\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.059 0.298 0.506 rg
42.5196850393700814 612.2837007874015853 Td
(1. Push the code repository from the current GitHub repository to the owner's personal GitHub account.) Tj
T* (2. Go to vercel.com, log in using the owner's GitHub, and import the repository.) Tj
T* (3. Add all the 16 environment variables listed in Section 2 in the Vercel project settings.) Tj
T* (4. Click Deploy to publish the website live.) Tj
T* (5. \(Optional\) Go to Settings > Domains, enter your custom domain name \(e.g. dayfoundation.org.in\), and configure the) Tj
T* (DNS settings provided by Vercel.) Tj
ET
